## Implementation Details
The Analytics component is configured in the root layout exactly as recommended in the official documentation:

```typescript
import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';

export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en" data-theme={theme} className={`${exo.variable} ${manrope.variable}`}>
      <body>
        <DevTools />
        <div className="glow" aria-hidden />
        <BrandHeader />
        <main className="container">{children}</main>
        <SiteFooter />
        <Analytics />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

The `<Analytics />` component is placed at the end of the `<body>` tag, which is the recommended location for optimal page load performance.

## Next Steps for Deployment
To enable Web Analytics on Vercel:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel (or redeploy if already deployed)
2. Navigate to the project's Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard
3. Click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics
4. After deployment, verify the analytics script loads by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to the analytics endpoint

